      "side": 1,
      "message": "if the `CONFIG_TEST_EXTRA_STACK_SIZE` is removed, you have stacking error\n\n```\nDEBUG:START - test_essential_thread\nDEBUG:[0.997000] \u003cerr\u003e os: ***** MPU FAULT *****\nDEBUG:[1.001000] \u003cerr\u003e os:   Stacking error (context area might be not valid)\nDEBUG:[1.007000] \u003cerr\u003e os:   Data Access Violation\nDEBUG:[1.011000] \u003cerr\u003e os:   MMFAR Address: 0x2001a6f4\nDEBUG:[1.016000] \u003cerr\u003e os: \u003e\u003e\u003e ZEPHYR FATAL ERROR 2: Stack overflow on CPU 0\nDEBUG:[1.022000] \u003cerr\u003e os: Current thread: 0x20002c58 (unknown)\nDEBUG:Caught system error -- reason 2 1\nDEBUG:Fatal error expected as part of test case.\nDEBUG:\nDEBUG:    Assertion failed at EC_BASE/zephyr/test/lib/src/exit.c:39: ztest_post_fatal_error_hook: reason not equal to K_ERR_KERNEL_PANIC\nDEBUG:\nDEBUG:[1.046000] \u003cerr\u003e os: ***** HARD FAULT *****\nDEBUG:[1.049000] \u003cerr\u003e os:   Fault escalation (see below)\nDEBUG:[1.054000] \u003cerr\u003e os: ARCH_EXCEPT with reason 4\nDEBUG:\nDEBUG:[1.058000] \u003cerr\u003e os: \u003e\u003e\u003e ZEPHYR FATAL ERROR 4: Kernel panic on CPU 0\nDEBUG:[1.064000] \u003cerr\u003e os: Fault during interrupt handling\nDEBUG:\nDEBUG:[1.069000] \u003cerr\u003e os: Current thread: 0x20002808 (unknown)\nDEBUG:Caught system error -- reason 4 0\nDEBUG:Fatal error was unexpected, aborting...\n```\n\nIt looks that in the Zephyr Real-Time Operating System (RTOS), `CONFIG_TEST_EXTRA_STACK_SIZE` is a configuration option primarily used within the Zephyr testing framework. Its purpose is to add extra stack space to threads created during tests.",
